---@field EndDate? aws.scheduler.EndDate The date, in UTC, before which the schedule can invoke its target. Depending on the schedule's recurrence expression, invocations might stop on, or before, the EndDate you specify. EventBridge Scheduler ignores EndDate for one-time schedules.
---@field Description? aws.scheduler.Description The description you specify for the schedule.
---@field ScheduleExpressionTimezone? aws.scheduler.ScheduleExpressionTimezone The timezone in which the scheduling expression is evaluated.
---@field State? aws.scheduler.ScheduleState Specifies whether the schedule is enabled or disabled.
---@field KmsKeyArn? aws.scheduler.KmsKeyArn The ARN for the customer managed KMS key that that you want EventBridge Scheduler to use to encrypt and decrypt your data.
---@field Target aws.scheduler.Target The schedule target. You can use this operation to change the target that your schedule invokes.
---@field FlexibleTimeWindow aws.scheduler.FlexibleTimeWindow Allows you to configure a time window during which EventBridge Scheduler invokes the schedule.
---@field ClientToken? aws.scheduler.ClientToken Unique, case-sensitive identifier you provide to ensure the idempotency of the request. If you do not specify a client token, EventBridge Scheduler uses a randomly generated token for the request to ensure idempotency.
---@field ActionAfterCompletion? aws.scheduler.ActionAfterCompletion Specifies the action that EventBridge Scheduler applies to the schedule after the schedule completes invoking the target.

